## Implementation Rules

- ✅ Use parameterized queries only (no string interpolation in SQL)
- ✅ Verify passwords with `werkzeug.security.check_password_hash(stored_hash, provided_password)`
- ✅ No SQLAlchemy or ORMs - raw SQL with `get_db()`
- ✅ Server-side validation for all fields
- ✅ Security best practice: Same error message for non-existent email and wrong password
- ✅ Preserve email on validation errors (not password)
- ✅ Use Flask's `session` for authentication state
- ✅ Use Flask's `flash()` for user feedback messages
- ✅ Use CSS variables (`.auth-success` class already defined)

